DDC single-leg-balance motions — data/data_stratified_900/
===========================================================

These motion clips (sample_<support>_<id>_mj.npz; Unitree G1 29-DoF, 50 Hz, 249 frames) are a
DERIVATIVE of the AMS synthetic balance-motion dataset:

  Pan et al., "Agility Meets Stability: Versatile Humanoid Control with Heterogeneous Data,"
  arXiv:2511.17373, 2025 (OpenDriveLab).
    dataset : https://huggingface.co/datasets/ruoyiqiao/AMS   (synthetic_balance_motions_10k.pkl)
    code    : https://github.com/OpenDriveLab/AMS

What we changed
---------------
From AMS's ~9,814 valid synthetic single-leg-balance clips we (1) retargeted the motions to the
Unitree G1 29-DoF MuJoCo model, and (2) distilled a compact, difficulty-stratified, balanced set of
900 clips — a 3x3 grid over support-leg squat depth (pelvis height) x swing-foot absolute height,
100 clips per class (50/50 left/right), split 720 train / 90 val / 90 test balanced across classes
and support sides (seed 42). Per-clip class / bin / support / split labels are in
data_stratified_900/dataset_info.json (and manifest.csv). See the DDC paper, Appendix E.

These modifications (retargeting + distillation) were made for DDC by the DDC authors in July 2026,
stated here as required for a GPL-3.0 derivative (GPL-3.0 §5(a): a modified work carries prominent
notices stating that it was changed, and the date).

